; four-way-run-recipe42.fk — the body's four-way proof, runnable in one command.
;
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/four-way-run.fk
;
; The body's own four-way proof, as a source cell: `.tbl` execution is retired,
; so this is the runnable entry.
;
; Run from the repository root:
;
;     ./fkwu proof/four-way-run-recipe42.fk        -> 0   (FOUR-WAY)
;
; fkwu host-execs the three minimal walkers on proof/recipe42.fk, reads their values, and
; hands all four to fwv-verdict: 0 FOUR-WAY / 1 FKWU-SUSPECT / 2 WALKER-SUSPECT.
;
; The three walker paths below are what walkers/README.md's own build lines produce, plus a
; node runner for the TS one. Built here 2026-07-25 from source, no prebuilt artifact:
;
;     cd walkers/go   && go build -o walker .
;     cd walkers/rust && cargo build --release
;     node --experimental-strip-types walkers/ts/main.ts <recipe>       (node 22; no tsx needed)
;
; Witnessed 2026-07-25, and perturbation-verified the same way the 2026-06-29 receipt did —
; the verdict is COMPUTED, not a constant:
;
;     all three walkers on recipe42, fkwu told 42   -> 0   FOUR-WAY
;     all three on recipe42, fkwu told 99           -> 1   FKWU-SUSPECT
;     ts pointed at a recipe answering 99           -> 2   WALKER-SUSPECT
;
; The fkwu value is passed in rather than computed here because fkwu is the one running this
; cell; ./fkwu proof/recipe42.fk answers 42 on its own, and that is the number below.

(do
    (fr-diagnose
        "./walkers/go/walker proof/recipe42.fk"
        "./walkers/rust/target/release/form-walker-rust proof/recipe42.fk"
        "node --experimental-strip-types walkers/ts/main.ts proof/recipe42.fk"
        42))
